{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"verdict\": \"discrepancy\",\n  \"statementAssessment\": \"The exposition claims the identity for every real x, while the formal proposition assumes x != 0. The unrestricted claim is false for totalized real division, where 0 / 0 = 0; under ordinary quotient notation, the expression at x = 0 is undefined.\",\n  \"methodAssessment\": \"The formal argument describes a valid restricted claim: for nonzero real x, x / x = 1. No proof steps or method are supplied to assess beyond that description.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"“For every real x, the quotient x/x equals 1.”\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"“The formal declaration assumes x!=0 and concludes x/x=1.”\",\n      \"classification\": \"discrepancy: source statement is false under totalized real division; formal proposition narrows its domain\",\n      \"explanation\": \"At x = 0, totalized real division gives 0 / 0 = 0, not 1. With ordinary quotient notation, x/x at zero is undefined. The formal assumption excludes this case.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The source says “For every real x”; the formal counterpart explicitly assumes x!=0. Taking x = 0 witnesses the failure under totalized real division.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"The input does not specify a division convention. Under ordinary quotient notation the zero case is undefined; under totalized real division it is a counterexample.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"examinedAssertions\": [\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“For every real x, the quotient x/x equals 1.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"Not valid as stated: the zero case is undefined or, under totalized real division, gives 0 rather than 1.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Substitute x = 0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"The formal declaration assumes x!=0 and concludes x/x=1.\",\n      \"assessment\": \"Faithful restricted identity; it does not correspond to the exposition’s unrestricted domain.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"For nonzero x, x/x = 1.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"omissions\": [\n    \"The exposition does not state a nonzero-domain restriction.\"\n  ],\n  \"toolsUsed\": [\n    \"Read /input/INPUT.md with a shell command.\"\n  ],\n  \"checkingStatus\": \"Mathematical reasoning only. No Lean checks were run; the input provides a rendered formal argument, not an original Lean module.\"\n}"}}
